// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-panics.py %S/Inputs/panics-gopp
// P04.05: the failures only Go++ has, each with exit status 2 and its first
// line on standard error after the output that came before:
// - a new key inserted into a map while a range over it runs (hidden from the
//   checker's RNG-3 by a call), also `mm[k1][k2] = v` with k1 absent: "panic:
//   map insert during iteration" every time (RNG-4: the map counts its running
//   ranges; break, return, goto and continue or break of an outer loop end
//   one, and writing a key that is there is no insert);
// - slicing an owned slice past its length, within its capacity, as a
//   re-slice in place or as a borrowed slice (SLC-13: the elements past the
//   length are not live): "slice bounds out of range [:5] with length 3";
// - `==` of two views of slices boxed in interfaces (P04.06: a boxed view
//   compares as the value it shows, and a slice does not compare):
//   "comparing uncomparable type View[[]int]".
// Inputs/panics-gopp/*.out and .err are written by hand: Go has no such
// program.
